      "content": "That's incredibly strong. It really strips away the excuses. \n\nOne thing I'm worried about is if someone asks me during the Q&A, \"But isn't it true that if all the candidates are corrupt, not voting is a valid way to deny them legitimacy?\" How should I respond to that using the same tone? I want a response that shuts down that line of thinking by explaining why that logic is inherently flawed and morally wrong.",
